Description: Offer no screenshots while the session is locked.
 GNOME Shell offers its screenshot UI on the lock screen, from the screenshot button in quick settings and
 with Print, and Shift+Print saves a screenshot of the whole screen there. Upstream keeps this on purpose:
 the lock screen shows nothing private, and screen recording, selecting a window and Alt+Print are already
 unavailable while locked. Anyone at the locked machine can still save screenshots into the user's Pictures
 folder and replace the user's clipboard contents with them, so here no screenshot is offered at all.
 .
 Print and Shift+Print are bound in the same restricted action modes as Alt+Print and screen recording, and
 the button is hidden while the session is locked. Quick settings stay the same across locking, so the
 button's visibility follows the session mode as it changes, as the settings button next to it does, and is
 no longer set once when the button is created.
Author: Mitar
Bug: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/gnome-shell/-/issues/9469
